{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"The consumer matches responses by the full `SystemCtx`; it does not map a newer context back to an older request. Term checks and sender-membership checks also appear to leave this case admissible. I’ll submit a deterministic exploration using real bootstrap, election, and follower forwarding, with the first read’s heartbeats dropped and subsequent messages delivered. The endpoint is response identity, not a claim of permanent client stalling.\n"}}
